#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Zorin XP — Windows XP's "Open" / "Save As" dialog.

A portal service (org.freedesktop.impl.portal.FileChooser) that
xdg-desktop-portal uses instead of GNOME's dialog: it serves flatpak
applications, browsers and, with GTK_USE_PORTAL=1 / GDK_DEBUG=portals, every
GTK application. The window follows comdlg32.dll's template 1552 (positions,
texts), with the places bar, the toolbar and XP's five views (Thumbnails,
Tiles, Icons, List, Details), the right-click menu, names edited in place,
XP's message boxes and the resize grip in the corner. The size and the view
are remembered from one time to the next (~/.local/share/zorin-xp/filechooser.json).

If something goes wrong when opening the window, the request goes to
GNOME's dialog (org.freedesktop.impl.portal.desktop.gnome): no application
is left unable to open or save.

Test without the portal:  zorin-xp-filechooser --test open|save|folder|multi [folder [name]]
(ZXP_FC_SCRIPT=<file.py> runs a test script with the window in `dlg`)
"""
